ntdll, ws2_32: Proton's compatibility switches

Switches for programs that depend on a detail of Windows or of the machine, read from the
environment under the names Proton gives them, so that what is known to help a game on Proton
can be used as it is. The app sets them for the games in Proton's own table (GameFixes.swift,
by Steam app id), and they can be set by hand in a prefix's or a program's variables.

  WINE_HEAP_DELAY_FREE=1       freed heap blocks are kept for a while before they are reused
  WINE_HEAP_ZERO_MEMORY=1      every heap hands out zeroed memory
  WINE_HEAP_TOP_DOWN=1         heaps are placed from the top of the address space down
  WINE_CPU_TOPOLOGY=n[:...]    no more than n processors are reported (Proton also pins the
                               program to the processors after the colon; macOS cannot)
  WINE_RAM_REPORTING_BIAS=n    n megabytes less memory is reported than there is
  WINE_DISABLE_SFN=1           files have no 8.3 short names
  WINE_BLOCK_HOSTS=a;b         host names under a or b are not found (up to 16)
  FINEWINE_HIDE_WINE_EXPORTS=1 wine_get_version, wine_get_build_id and wine_get_host_version
                               are not found by name in ntdll, for programs that refuse to run
                               on Wine. The runtime's own parts ask for the first and the last
                               as __finewine_get_version and __finewine_get_host_version, two
                               new names for the same functions that stay (FEX patch 0015).

Left out of what Proton has: WINE_SIMULATE_WRITECOPY (it builds on Proton's tracking of
write-copy pages, which this Wine does not have), WINE_LARGE_ADDRESS_AWARE (32-bit programs
here have the whole 4 GB window already), and the switches for Linux's synchronisation and
window system.

Tested by tests/runtime/compat-switches.c on ARM64, x64 and 32-bit, with the switches and
without.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/heap.c b/dlls/ntdll/heap.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/heap.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/heap.c
@@ -968,6 +968,17 @@
